The tire this scene's robot rolls is the tire of drcl-deploy/assets
(https://github.com/drcl-deploy/assets, at 90e2260): its mesh, and the eight convex parts
it collides with. The repository's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md states:

    "The MIT license at the repository root covers original project code. Bundled
     third-party models, meshes, textures, and derived files remain under their
     respective upstream terms."

and it records no source or terms for the tire. Finding no terms for redistributing it,
this demo holds it to those it follows for the curb scene's GRAIL data, the Creative
Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 license's, and takes it down at an owner's request.

Changed here: the tire is drawn in one gray, without its tread texture, and this scene
builds it into its model.

The license's terms are at

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

It permits sharing and adapting for noncommercial purposes only, with credit.
